    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0175" n="163" xml:id="pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6151/51: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-21T13:00:00+03:00">March 21, 1941—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>561. The Moscow press this morning publishes a Tass announcement that A. E.
                        Bogomolov,<anchor n="18" xml:id="d172-f1"/> the present Soviet Chargé
                    d’Affaires in Vichy, has been appointed Soviet Ambassador to France. The post
                    has been vacant since the recall last year of Surits<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d172-f2"/> at the request of the French Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d172-f1" n="18" xml:id="d172-f1-content">
                <p>Alexander Efremovich Bogomolov.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d172-f2" n="19" xml:id="d172-f2-content">
                <p>Yakov Zakharovich Surits (Suritz) had been declared <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >persona non grata</hi> in March 1940.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
